  "normativeRationale": "The unchanged approved CAP-05.S01.T01 contract requires actual native picker/drop selection and bounded local document attachment within the existing Ingestion and Reconciliation workflow. Accepted ADR-0003, approved RO-UI-ACADEMIC-MINIMAL-1.8, and the adopted A01/A02/A03 authority retain native selection, explicit rights and association, local Core/project boundaries, truthful status and failure recovery, and researcher authority. The resumed renderer preserves those approved decisions: inspected candidates remain drafts until explicit association; unknown or denied rights do not permit commit; Cancel/Escape and project-lock/restart recovery retain the established context. The native restoration recognizes only the exact disabled and transparent noninteractive graphics leaf, checks the live owned root/ancestry/identities, omits that leaf from OLE registration, and retains denial and rollback. The final generic unavailable message stops making an unsupported claim that no file was selected or attached and does not infer a native-bridge cause from a Core rejection. These changes restore approved functional and truthful failure behavior within the existing workspace. They introduce no governed workflow, route, design language, filesystem authority, private-data egress, implicit plugin grant, remote write or researcher decision. This semantic judgment does not establish the separate full-history continuation gate as passed.",
